       "El equipo más importante son tus ojos.",
       "p-eyes"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Language focus",
     "title": "What is it for? used to / used for",
     "steps": [
      [
       "used to + verb",
       "The echo sounder is used to measure the depth."
      ],
      [
       "used for + -ing",
       "The radar is used for watching other ships."
      ],
      [
       "question",
       "What is it used for?"
      ]
     ],
     "paras": [
      "Two ways to say what equipment is <b>for</b>: <b>is used to</b> + verb, or <b>is used for</b> + verb<b>-ing</b>. Same meaning.",
      "Short and natural on the bridge: <i>It shows other ships.</i> <i>It measures the depth.</i> (Remember the -s from Lesson 4.)"
     ],
     "avoid": "It's used for measure the depth. · It's used to measuring. · It serves for…"
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "The echo sounder is used to ___ the depth.",
     "opts": [
      "measure",
      "measuring",
      "measures"
     ],
     "a": 0
    },
    {
